{"index":1580,"node_id":"27863099-3142-4f54-8ce7-120b753eaff8","parent":"585f616a-f01c-4dba-9f4d-690088e20244","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791089311.423824,"update_time":1791089326.051792,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Changed the old reading-room controller into a **Comprehension Task Controller**.\n\nNow a change to `read-request.json` causes the workflow to instantiate `task_semantic_define_each_array_item.json`, bind its target to `agentsmdbaseproejction.json`, and publish that instantiated task through the same control location the reading-room workflow used. fileciteturn414file0L2-L6\n\nI added a dedicated controller script that handles the task lifecycle. It calculates the four readiness Booleans against the real projection, uses the existing flatten checker, applies your terminal-`{}`/`[]` empty rule, calculates the expected nonempty count independently, and verifies the completed archive. PASS requires exactly the expected number of records and every record must be definition-only:\n\n```json\n{\"item\":\"semantic definition\"}\n```\n\nNo retry is performed on failure; it produces `FAILED`. Successful completion produces `PASS`. fileciteturn415file0L2-L6\n\nThe old PNG issuing, `sharp`, card manifests, cache restoration, locator verification, and fresh-challenge-on-failure behavior are no longer in the workflow. The workflow now has only **issue task → submit completed task → verify completion → PASS/FAILED**. fileciteturn414file0L2-L6\n\nCommits:\n\n- Controller script: `b3f9a2c557d5c50dcd84c333157f52d3dd8f8d83`\n- Workflow replacement: `8698333c756d8626d20d03d541cce3c88ecbb965`\n\nI did **not** trigger a task run; this only changes the controller/runtime."}
